    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταυροπόλος</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>IT</u>
			1457
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Lys.</u>
			447
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>CIG</u>
			2699
		</span></i> (<span class="entity">Mylasa</span>); also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταυροπόλα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>Aj.</u>
			172
		</span></i> (lyr.):—a name of Artemis (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ταυρώ</span>), variously interpreted as <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>worshipped at Tauris</i>, or <i>drawn by a
				yoke of bulls</i>, or <i>hunting bulls</i>; cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ister
				8
			</span></i>; applied to Iphigenia, Ant. <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				27.3
			</span></i>.</div>
